Open Risks
---------

- CSN snapshots still lose their boundary when exported, imported, or
  serialized through the current transport helpers.
- `pg_csnlog` truncation still depends on the runtime and legacy horizons
  visible at vacuum time, so truncation safety must stay covered by tests
  that exercise both the live horizon and restart paths.
- Restart and prepared-transaction paths are conservative, but not yet backed
  by a restart-stable CSN retention contract.
- Subxid overflow remains a risk until the fallback and parent-resolution
  behavior is closed out under explicit tests.
- Any future Stage 2 work must keep the current "no silent downgrade" rule:
  if a path cannot preserve `snapshot_csn`, it must fail or be explicitly
  forbidden for CSN-sensitive snapshots.

